    "effectivePlan" : "Play D3 and win the opening lead in South. There are eight top tricks: three clubs, two diamonds, two hearts and one spade. Seek a fourth club while limiting concessions to one. Cash CA, then lead a low club toward dummy. If West follows to the second club, play CQ; continue clubs toward CK and establish the long clubs, conceding one trick if necessary. If West shows out on the second club after following initially, play C7 instead of CQ: concede to East while preserving CQ and CK to capture East's remaining clubs. Retain the second diamond honor and the heart and spade controls to regain the lead after the club concession; dummy's HK also provides an entry if needed. This safety line secures four club tricks against every 3–2 or 4–1 split, giving nine tricks overall. If clubs prove 5–0, reassess the development and entries rather than assuming four club tricks. Prefer securing the contract to risking it for a fifth club trick.",
